          "caption": "The Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture's building at 515 Malcolm X. Boulevard (Lenox Avenue) was constructed between 1969 and 1980, and opened to the public in 1978.  It was designed by Bond Ryder Associates.  A link to the Center's original building, the former 135th Street Branch, was built in 1991, designed by Davis Brody Bond.  The building was renovated in 2007. (Source: 'AIA Guide to NYC (5th ed.))",
